Files under this directory were imported from libiap(https://github.com/mojyack/libiap) except for:
- README.rockbox: this file, Rockbox specific notes
- HEAD: libiap commit hash

To sync with the upstream, use ../libiap-sync.sh script.

Local changes
-------------
This copy is not identical to libiap at HEAD: Rockbox changes it for car
head units (tested with a Volvo XC40), and these changes are not upstream
yet:
- identification: IDPS with deferred or no authentication, Identify and
  IdentifyDeviceLingoes, unknown FID tokens accepted
- General, Display Remote and Extended Interface queries head units send
  (lingo options, UI mode, event notifications, EQ profiles, sound check,
  localization, iTunes DB info, protocol version, artwork)
- database access: select, reset, count and record streaming, with the
  platform callbacks in platform.h
- next/previous album and playlist controls
- restore-on-exit for SetRepeat and SetShuffle
- a request arriving while a response spanning several HID reports is
  still being sent is answered after it (iap.c, hid.c)
- swap_64() and unaligned stores fixed
- RequestIPodName answers with the name in .rockbox/playername.txt

libiap-sync.sh refuses to overwrite this directory while it differs from
upstream at HEAD. To update libiap, port these changes onto the new
upstream (or get them merged there), then sync with --force.
